    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **42 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 including the new `Cp29Tests` (postcode) and `Cp13Tests` (which exercises differing postcodes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, city-validated `postcode` field for owners. Changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` string property to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since it lives in `OwnerFields` (not read-only), the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` accepts it on create and `OwnerDto` returns it on read.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` field (`@Column(name = \"postcode\")`) with getter/setter, so it's persisted and mapped.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added a `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Added a `validatePostcode(city, postcode)` call plus the helper and fixed lookup tables:\n   - Absent/empty postcode \u2192 skipped (backward-compatible; owner still accepted).\n   - Present but not exactly 4 digits \u2192 `400`.\n   - Present and city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) but out of that region's inclusive range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) \u2192 `400`.\n   - Present, 4 digits, city with no known region \u2192 accepted (permissive default).\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `postcode` automatically by name in both directions, so a stored postcode is returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Rejections reuse the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (\u2192 400), consistent with the surrounding validation style.",
